# TODO - Commit hooks and contribution gates

## Objective

Verify contribution validation and activate the repository hooks.

## Acceptance

- Test pre-commit and commit-msg hooks using isolated temporary fixtures.
- Reject invalid Conventional Commits and missing or invalid DCO trailers.
- Require a lowercase kebab-case scope and a subject of at most 72 characters.
- Validate all reachable HEAD messages with the same prospective policy.
- Reject staged non-distributable files and keep commit checks reusable.
- Activate local hooks and validate each signed Conventional Commit.

## Evidence

Fresh validation passed on 2026-11-24 in run
1795575589898921939-2506275 (73 tests). Rust fixtures validate positive and
negative commit subjects, mandatory scope, 72-character maximum, DCO
trailer syntax, staged file paths and reachable commit-history framing.
Unix temporary fixtures execute both actual hook scripts with isolated
command delegates, verifying dispatch arguments, ordering and rejection
when either validation subprocess fails.

Local `core.hooksPath` is `.githooks`. Both executable hooks ran successfully
on signed commits `edb3142` and `3a170c9`; the fresh validation history
check accepted every reachable HEAD commit. Both commits were pushed to
`origin/main`. This policy validates DCO syntax, not identity ownership.
